<http://data.silknow.org/object/895ea5d6-64db-3c4b-b048-549c65df85f7/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Turban-cloth('pag') of red silk with woven gold-wrapped thread. 'Lungi' is a term which can be applied to both waistcloths and turbans depending on the locality, but in Punjab refers only to waistcloths, while a turban is call 'pag'.  Silk has not traditionally been cultivated in Punjab but imported from other areas such as Bukhara, Khorasan, and Bengal."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/895ea5d6-64db-3c4b-b048-549c65df85f7> .

